{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-10-26","kind":"proposition","title":"性质与证明：中项无理线段与比例","englishTitle":"4 medial area does not exceed a medial area by a rational area.","book":10,"number":26,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26/","group":"prop_1","sourceNumber":26,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":null}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","contentId":"euclid-10-26","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"0fbdeb900c3b892346d9085087acb1734ce34330bf41caccebbaa5dfddddcea9","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-10-26.statement","euclid-10-26.proof.1","euclid-10-26.proof.2","euclid-10-26.proof.3","euclid-10-26.proof.4","euclid-10-26.proof.5","euclid-10-26.proof.6","euclid-10-26.proof.7","euclid-10-26.proof.8","euclid-10-26.proof.9","euclid-10-26.proof.10","euclid-10-26.proof.11","euclid-10-26.conclusion","euclid-10-26.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-10-26.statement","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"ff86cfe4e91146e9f67347554e683896c4358a4f940dbd439a4890ea22d63e6e","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"4 medial area does not exceed a medial area by a rational area."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"4 中项无理线段个区域不超过中项无理线段个区域有理面积个区域。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":1,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"905e2da41183a79212ac7a02d4460b81b489d41c317fb5754c7c8b0592773c41","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let the medial area AB exceed the medial area AC by the rational area DB, and let a rational straight line EF be set out; to EF let there be applied the rectangular parallelogram FH equal to AB, producing EH as breadth, and let the rectangle FG equal to AC be subtracted; therefore the remainder BD is equal to the remainder KH."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能,让中项无理线段区域AB超出中项无理线段区域AC,再加有理面积、DB,再加有理线段、EF;EF让应用长方形平行四边形、FH等于AB,宽度扩大EH,再减去矩形、FG等于AC;因此,其余BD等于其余KH。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"7f53e59c99eaad656295cd8e7a036269f9fa39fcb47df6a9b435c13a59a772c5","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But DB is rational; therefore KH is also rational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但DB是有理,因此KH也是有理。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"a1ad7e2c9e7704c9a3b944dd54bfcc1674d7741b78ae00dafd562a5695bb7238","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Since, then, each of the rectangles AB, AC is medial, and AB is equal to FH, and AC to FG, therefore each of the rectangles FH, FG is also medial."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"从那时起,矩形 AB中,AC各为中项无理线段,AB等于FH,AC等于FG,因此,矩形 FH中,FG也是中项无理线段。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"3abc2287d0a2d3550cc85e98e420d3dce2c1d1409dfcf126cb0af4e4f222c8c1","citations":["euclid-10-22"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And they are applied to the rational straight line EF; therefore each of the straight lines HE, EG is rational and incommensurable in length with EF. [[X. 22](/principles/euclid-10-22)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"适用于有理线段 EF;因此,HE直线、EG直线和不可公度直线各长EF。 [[X. 22](/principles/euclid-10-22)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"69a8029b2fbec282df1634bc7676422980f9bac89c4600758324fc4e910bcd7d","citations":["euclid-10-20"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, since [DB is rational and is equal to KH, therefore] KH is [also] rational; and it is applied to the rational straight line EF; therefore GH is rational and commensurable in length with EF. [[X. 20](/principles/euclid-10-20)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"由于[DB是有理,等于KH,因此]KH是[也]有理;适用于有理线段 EF;因此,GH是有理,长度可公度是EF。 [[X. 20](/principles/euclid-10-20)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.6","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 6","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"bdd94c91866a467cfe8c54db9983086ea89e60df8a4d76699ccb8e2e4c2f1b4a","citations":["euclid-10-13"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But EG is also rational, and is incommensurable in length with EF; therefore EG is incommensurable in length with GH. [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但EG也是有理,不可公度是EF,因此EG是不可公度,GH。 [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.7","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":7,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 7","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5467941402f476b553c37705d6ab1421e54b737bf3ee255a713eb1b8320673ce","citations":["euclid-10-11"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"And, as EG is to GH, so is the square on EG to the rectangle EG, GH; therefore the square on EG is incommensurable with the rectangle EG, GH. [[X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"EG比GH等于EG比正方形比矩形,EG比GH,因此EG比正方形等于不可公度比不可公度,GH [[X. 11](/principles/euclid-10-11)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.8","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":8,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 8","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"871250a6757ea8df02407881c2197070e630b340cdce95ab8a20949f7153a81d","citations":["euclid-10-6","euclid-10-13","euclid-2-4","euclid-10-16"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on EG, GH are commensurable with the square on EG, for both are rational; and twice the rectangle EG, GH is commensurable with the rectangle EG, GH, for it is double of it; [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)] therefore the squares on EG, GH are incommensurable with twice the rectangle EG, GH; [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)] therefore also the sum of the squares on EG, GH and twice the rectangle EG, GH, that is, the square on EH [[II. 4](/principles/euclid-2-4)], is incommensurable with the squares on EG, GH. [[X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但是,EG,GH,可公度,EG,正方形,有理;矩形,EG,GH,可公度,可公度,矩形,EG,GH,223,EG,EG,正方形,EG,不可公度,不可公度,不可公度,223,GH;因此,EG和GH的正方形和矩形和EG的两倍,即EH和GH的正方形和不可公度和GH的两倍,是不可公度和正方形和EG和GH的不可公度和不可公度和GH。 [[X. 6](/principles/euclid-10-6)] [[X. 13](/principles/euclid-10-13)] [[II. 4](/principles/euclid-2-4)] [[X. 16](/principles/euclid-10-16)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.9","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":9,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 9","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"01a8ea5b9d3ec1ce5c15203da6a850b20acc0ce34ba601c3fdbbe13c7aca8476","citations":["euclid-10-def-4"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But the squares on EG, GH are rational; therefore the square on EH is irrational. [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但EG,GH的正方形是有理,EH的正方形是无理。 [[X. Def. 4](/principles/euclid-10-def-4)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.10","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":10,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 10","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5b3518e0c850deb48594673388c30939fef7678b6f6486c6f69c29ea5c4e91c8","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore EH is irrational."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"所以EH是无理"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.proof.11","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":11,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 11","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9f137ff60f38014a0b4b6bdbf8227d0656a0d138febecd471a20cd7cafec5dbd","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But it is also rational: which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"但它也是有理: 这是不可能的。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":12,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-10-26.source","contentId":"euclid-10-26","revisionId":"euclid-10-26@raw-0fbdeb900c3b8923","order":13,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"9c9ebf03265f7b127844f43de9ff2f2698aae13cc5b2be3c1e14be25659b5acf","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-10-26:euclid-10-22:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-10-26","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-10-26.proof.4"],"targetContentId":"euclid-10-22","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:10.prop_1.26/","sourceLabel":"X. 22"}},{"id":"edge:euclid-10-26:euclid-10-20:explicit","sour